From aade2045a2addcd4d3b7491399440014362e42d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beau4201 <beau.ten.berge@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:10:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] resolver: never cache or serve an answer for a name of the
 exit mask list

The answer cache of the resolver is kept per network and shared by every uid,
and a cache hit sends no packet. The exit service of Compartments answers the
DNS queries of an app of class Masked itself for the names of its mask list,
but only when the query leaves the phone; a real answer that another uid had
cached reached the masked app without the exit service seeing the query, and a
fake answer of the exit service reached an app that is not masked (NET-014).

resolv_cache_lookup now returns RESOLV_CACHE_SKIP and resolv_cache_add refuses
for a query with a question name on the list. The list is the read-only file
of the system image that the exit service reads, loaded once on the first query
by the new ExitMaskList, which matches by the rules of the service: the row of
the longest domain that the name is, or is below, decides, and a protected row
(company 0) shields. A file that is missing or is not a list leaves the list
empty, so the cache stays as it is.
---
 Android.bp       |   1 +
 ExitMaskList.cpp | 170 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 ExitMaskList.h   |  66 ++++++++++++++++++
 res_cache.cpp    |  28 ++++++++
 4 files changed, 265 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 ExitMaskList.cpp
 create mode 100644 ExitMaskList.h

